# Theme, Accent & UI Consistency

When implementing new UI, **respect the global theme system** so light/dark mode and user-selected accent colors work without per-feature overrides.

Theme is applied at app root via `applyTheme()` (`@/shared/utils/core.ts`): `document.documentElement` gets `.light` / `.dark` and `data-accent-color`. Tokens live in `front-end/src/styles/globals.css`.

## Token layers (use in this order)

| Layer | Use for | Examples |
|-------|---------|----------|
| **Semantic** | Base surfaces and text | `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-card` |
| **Glass** | Cards, panels, filters, dialogs | `bg-[var(--glass-bg)]`, `border-[var(--glass-border)]`, `shadow-[var(--glass-shadow)]` |
| **Accent (user-selectable)** | CTAs, highlights, active states, links | `var(--accent-primary)`, `--accent-text`, `--accent-bg`, `--accent-border`, `--accent-button-text` |
| **Destructive** | Delete / irreversible actions only | [delete-destructive-actions.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/delete-destructive-actions.mdc) — `Button variant="destructive"` |
| **Status** | Lifecycle/domain labels | [status-badges.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/status-badges.mdc) — `statusBadgeClasses` |

Do **not** mix layers: accent red is not delete red; status green is not accent green.

## Accent usage

- **Primary actions:** `Button variant="accent"` (default in `@/components/ui/button.tsx`).
- **Secondary / cancel:** `Button variant="outline"` with glass border: `border-[var(--glass-border)]`.
- **Selected / active UI:** `bg-[var(--accent-bg)] border-[var(--accent-border)] text-[var(--accent-text)]`.
- **Icons & emphasis:** `text-[var(--accent-text)]` or `text-[var(--accent-primary)]`.
- **Custom gradients:** only when matching existing patterns — use `from-[var(--accent-secondary)] to-[var(--accent-primary)]` and hover vars; never hardcode `#f97316` / `orange-500`.

Reference CSS variables: `--accent-primary`, `--accent-primary-hover`, `--accent-secondary`, `--accent-bg`, `--accent-border`, `--accent-text`, `--accent-button-text`.

## Do not

- Hardcode theme-specific colors (`bg-gray-900`, `text-white`, `#dc2626`, `dark:bg-slate-800`) when a token exists.
- Set inline `style={{ color: … }}` or fixed hex backgrounds for brand/accent UI (exception: data viz or third-party embeds).
- Call `applyTheme` or mutate root theme classes inside feature components — settings/app shell owns that.
- Add new accent palette keys without updating `globals.css`, `applyTheme` color map, and Settings/Showcase pickers.
- Use Tailwind `accent` / `primary` shadcn tokens for user-accent CTAs when `--accent-*` vars are intended.

## Reuse before inventing

Match neighboring pages and scoped rules:

- List pages → [list-page-shell.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/list-page-shell.mdc)
- Dialogs → [dialog-windows.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/dialog-windows.mdc)
- Cards → [list-card-layout.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/list-card-layout.mdc)
- Empty states → [empty-state-component.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/empty-state-component.mdc)
- Reusable cards → [component-showcase.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/component-showcase.mdc)

Prefer `@/components/ui/*` (Button, Card, Badge, Input) over bespoke styled elements.

## Typography & spacing

- Page titles: `text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground`; descriptions: `text-muted-foreground`.
- Body copy: `text-foreground`; supporting text: `text-muted-foreground`.
- Page padding: `p-4 lg:p-6` on list/detail shells (see list-page-shell).
- Transitions: `transition-all duration-200` on interactive cards/hover states where siblings use it.

## Before you finish a feature

1. Grep changed files for hardcoded palette classes (`orange-`, `red-5`, `gray-9`, `#` hex in className).
2. Confirm primary buttons use `variant="accent"` and destructive actions use destructive tokens.
3. Switch **light ↔ dark** and **each accent color** in Settings (or `/system/showcase` Primary tab) — no broken contrast or stuck orange-only styling.

## Verification

```bash
cd front-end
npm run type-check
npm run lint
```

Manual: Settings → Theme + Accent, then open the new/changed screens.

